claimed: okay-script-real-certs -- operator ask 2026-09-07: support properly signed certificates too. Three real gaps behind that sentence. (1) okay-tls's contextOf builds the private key with KeyFactory RSA ONLY, so a modern CA-issued EC key (Let's Encrypt's --key-type ecdsa, and its default for new accounts) fails at load: read the algorithm from the PKCS#8 DER instead (RSA, EC, Ed25519), with a named refusal for an encrypted key. (2) a fullchain.pem (leaf + intermediates) must load as a CHAIN -- generateCertificates already reads them all, but nothing proved it, and a chain in the wrong order is a handshake a browser refuses. (3) renewal: a CA cert lives 90 days, so Tls.reloading(cert, key, secrets) answers an SSLContext whose key manager re-reads the files when their mtime changes -- certbot renews, the site picks it up, no restart; OKAY_TLS_RELOAD=<seconds> in Serve. Touches okay-tls/Tls.scala, Serve.scala, specs/tls.md + specs/okay-script.md, docs; Live tests over an EC identity and over a renewed one.
